# US market calibration set (Market-Readiness Gate).
# One candidate per line with a KNOWN outcome. The probe runs these through the real
# pipeline in the US market and measures whether the engine can (a) find evidence there
# and (b) read it correctly. Expected outcomes are chosen to be decidable from public
# US evidence alone — if an entry needs UK knowledge to judge, it belongs in uk.jsonl.
#
# Half must be expected-PASS and half expected-KILL, or discrimination is satisfied by
# an engine that answers the same way every time (enforced in markets.load_calibration_set).
